{% extends "layout/gates.twig" %}
{% import "partials/article.twig" as art %}

{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE METHODOLOGY — how a winner is decided
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Half of a pair. /philosophy argues; this page enforces. Each ends by handing the
  reader to the other, which is what makes them one Integrity Centre rather than
  two pages that happen to share a stylesheet.

  ── WHY THE PHILOSOPHY IS ONLY A PRÉCIS HERE ────────────────────────────────

  The full argument used to open this page: sixteen sections before the first
  table. That put Ubuntu between a reader arriving from a ballot and the answer to
  the question they came with, which is "how is a winner decided". So the argument
  moved to its own page and what stays is
  {@see CommunityVotingPhilosophy::summary()} — about four hundred words, enough
  that the {community_pct}/{judge_pct} split does not read as an unexplained hedge,
  with a door to the whole of it.

  It is a PRÉCIS, not an excerpt: a separate rendering written to stand alone at
  this length, carrying the same {tokens} so it cannot quote a figure the engine
  has changed.

  ── EVERY NUMBER ON THIS PAGE IS READ, NOT TYPED ────────────────────────────

  The weights, the bonus-vote ceiling, the judge quorum, the fraud bands and the
  community-return share all arrive from RuleEngine via the route — the same
  object the scorer consults. An operator can change any of them per programme and
  per cycle, and of every page on this site the METHODOLOGY page is the one that
  must not go on describing a system the code has stopped running.

  `default()` on each figure below is a rendering guard, not a published number: if
  the engine is unreachable the page must still say something coherent.

  ── NO COPY, NO DOWNLOAD, ON PURPOSE ────────────────────────────────────────

  Cite only. This page's prose lives in this template rather than in PHP, so there
  is no .txt or .md that IS this page — and a Download that saved a different
  document would be worse than no Download, because the reader would file it and
  find out later. {@see MethodologyDocument} for when that changes.
#}

