{#
  A FAQPage, built from questions this page VISIBLY ANSWERS. That constraint is the
  whole discipline: marking up an answer the reader cannot find is the thing search
  engines penalise, and it is also just a lie told in a format nobody reads.

  The figures interpolate from the same route variables the visible copy uses, so
  the machine-readable answer and the human one cannot drift — and a cycle override
  changes both at once.
#}
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}" type="application/ld+json">
{% set faq = [
  {
    q: 'How is the Cultural Power Index calculated?',
    a: 'The CPI is ' ~ community_pct|default(45) ~ '% verified community votes and ' ~ judge_pct|default(55) ~ '% independent judge panel. The community share is normalised within each category, so a nominee in a small category is measured against their own field rather than against the whole platform.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you buy votes to win an Africa GATES award?',
    a: 'No. Contributions add to a nominee’s public tally but are held in a separate column the scorer never reads, they cannot break a tie, and they are capped at ' ~ paid_cap_pct|default(50) ~ '% of the organic support a nominee has earned. Money can make a nominee look more popular; it cannot make them win.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Why might the nominee with the most votes not win?',
    a: 'Winning also requires at least ' ~ min_judges|default(2) ~ ' complete judge scorecards. A partial scorecard counts as nothing, judges recuse themselves from nominees they are connected to, and if nobody in a category reaches the quorum the award is not given.'
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens if two nominees tie?',
    a: 'The tiebreak is organic votes — the free, code-verified ones. Contributions are not consulted, so the closest possible race is decided by people rather than by spending. A tie on both the index and organic votes is recorded as a dead heat and escalated to the integrity team.'
  },
  {
    q: 'How do you know the results were not edited afterwards?',
    a: 'Every computed standing is sealed with a fingerprint of itself and of the record before it, so editing an old result breaks every record after it. The chain is re-verified automatically every day, and the database refuses to record two standings claiming the same predecessor.'
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the Africa GATES community return?',
    a: 'A nominee keeps ' ~ return_pct|default('50') ~ '% of what supporters contribute in their name, win or lose, once they have gathered ' ~ return_threshold|default(250) ~ ' votes of qualifying support. No single supporter can supply more than ' ~ return_cap_pct|default(10) ~ '% of that threshold, so qualifying takes at least ' ~ return_people|default(10) ~ ' different verified people.'
  }
] %}
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{% for f in faq %}{"@type":"Question","name":{{ f.q|json_encode|raw }},"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":{{ f.a|json_encode|raw }}}}{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}{% endfor %}]}
</script>
